    <string name="v5_help_t_measure">Measuring and calibration</string>
    <string name="v5_help_b_measure">In the Comment tab pick Measure. Distance takes two taps, perimeter and area several points then Done, circle the centre then a point on the edge, angle three points, count one tap per item. Tap the scale to type a ratio such as 1:100 or 1 cm = 2 m, or calibrate by drawing over a known length. Snapping sticks to line ends, intersections and glyph corners; drag with one finger to get the loupe. Measurements are saved as real measure annotations (/Measure) and can be exported to CSV.</string>
    <string name="v5_help_t_comments">Callouts, typewriter and marks</string>
    <string name="v5_help_b_comments">Callout: tap the arrow tip, then two corners of the box. Typewriter: tap where you want to type. Tick and cross take one tap, area highlight two corners, and line or arrow two points with a dash style and line endings.</string>
    <string name="v5_help_t_manager">Comment manager</string>
    <string name="v5_help_b_manager">Search comments and filter them by author, type, status and page, sort them and tick them with a private checkmark. Export to CSV, Word or a summary, or export only the highlighted text.</string>
    <string name="v5_help_t_stamps">Dynamic stamps</string>
    <string name="v5_help_b_stamps">Dynamic stamps fill in your name, title, organisation, date, time and Hijri date. Make your own templates with {name}, {date} and {hijri}. The sign-here set has: sign here, initial here, accepted, rejected, witness.</string>
    <string name="v5_help_t_reflow">Reflow reading</string>
    <string name="v5_help_b_reflow">Shows the whole document as flowing text with headings, paragraphs and images, with font size, line spacing, serif, justify, search and a headings list.</string>
    <string name="v5_help_t_split">Split view and compare</string>
    <string name="v5_help_b_split">Split the view to see two parts of the document at once, or compare two documents side by side with synced scrolling. Drag the divider to resize.</string>
    <string name="v5_help_t_present">Presentation</string>
    <string name="v5_help_b_present">Full screen with page transitions. Tap the edges or swipe to move, long-press for the laser pointer. Auto-advance and loop are available.</string>
    <string name="v5_help_t_overlays">Rulers, grid, reading ruler and lens</string>
    <string name="v5_help_b_overlays">From the View tab turn on centimetre rulers and the grid, the reading ruler that highlights a line and dims the rest, and the lens that magnifies what is under your finger.</string>
    <string name="v5_help_t_history">Auto-scroll and position history</string>
    <string name="v5_help_b_history">Auto-scroll moves the pages at the speed you choose. After every jump (link, outline, search) a button takes you back, and you can move back and forward through positions.</string>
    <string name="v5_help_t_commands">Command search and keyboard shortcuts</string>
    <string name="v5_help_b_commands">Type what you want to do in Tell me to find the command, long-press to pin it to the top bar. With a keyboard: Ctrl+K for command search and Ctrl+/ for the list of shortcuts. Long-press the app icon for quick shortcuts.</string>
    <string name="v5_help_t_trash">Trash</string>
    <string name="v5_help_b_trash">Files deleted from Files go to the trash for 30 days; you can restore them or delete them for good.</string>
    <string name="v5_help_t_print">Print options</string>
    <string name="v5_help_b_print">Choose the page range, odd or even pages and reverse order, print several pages per sheet or a folded booklet with right or left binding, with or without comments.</string>
    <string name="v5_help_t_tts">Read aloud</string>
    <string name="v5_help_b_tts">You can repeat the page or the whole document. Reading pauses for a phone call, other audio or unplugged headphones, and resumes after the call.</string>
